      "message": "[From Jetski review] If a target specifies `public \u003d [ \"$target_gen_dir/foo.h\" ]` (so `all_headers_public_` is `false`) and also lists the same generated header in `sources` (or `inputs`), and has no dependency on its generator at all, `Target::CheckSourcesGenerated()` will record `foo.h` twice: once as `PUBLIC_DEP` (from `public_headers_`) and once as `PRIVATE_DEP` (from `sources_` hitting the `else` branch).\n\nHere, `foo.h` will end up in both `missing.needs_public_dep[generator]` and `missing.needs_private_dep[generator]`, causing the same file to be printed twice under two different sections in the error message.\n\nConsider either skipping files in `sources_` that are already in `public_headers_`, or filtering out files already present in `missing.needs_public_dep` (or `should_be_public`) from `missing.needs_private_dep`.",
